ADCT uses partition schemes and a fast coding of binary digits numbers.
ADCT is FREE for scientific use.
It is a research version (only for Photoshop grayscale RAW images coding).

ADCT e <input file> <output file> <Quantization Step> [Width] - encode.
ADCT d <input file> <output file> - decode.
ADCT w <input file> <output file> - decode without deblocking.
ADCT p <first RAW file> <second RAW file> [Width] - calculation of PSNR.

Examples of usage:
adct e lena.raw lena.agu 40
adct e lena.raw lena.agu 40 512
adct d lena.agu lena_new.raw
adct w lena.agu lena_new.raw
adct p lena.raw lena_new.raw

Smaller value of quantization step provides better quality of decoded image.
